11
01:02:56,666 --> 01:03:02,666
It stars Christopher Walken, Laurence Fishburne, David Caruso, Victor Argo and Wesley Snipes, with supporting
roles played by Giancarlo Esposito, Steve Buscemi, Paul Calderón, Janet Julian and Theresa Randle.

12
01:08:40,000 --> 01:08:46,000
Walken portrays Frank White, a New York City drug kingpin rebuilding his criminal empire
after his release from prison, while also attempting to go legitimate.

13
01:14:23,333 --> 01:14:29,333
The film was released by Carolco Pictures (through New
Line Cinema) on September 28, 1990.

14
01:20:06,666 --> 01:20:12,666
It received mixed reviews from critics, with several
criticizing the film's violence and dark tone.

15
01:25:50,000 --> 01:25:56,000
Retrospective reviews have been much more positive, and the
film has been described as one of Ferrara's best.

16
01:31:33,333 --> 01:31:39,333
The film explores themes of new york city, gangster,
release from prison, hope, cocaine.

17
01:37:16,666 --> 01:37:22,666
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
